export anchor NOCWallStyle:
    number: 321
    screen: OpsMonitor
    name: NOC wall
    idea: A network operations video wall where every block is a square cornered screen split by black bezels, with huge status words, giant figures and thick chart lines that can be read from across the room.
    base: dark
    palette:
        bezel: #000000, the page and the 4px gaps between screens
        screen: #13161b, every tile and the style sheet
        screenRaised: #1c2027, the title strip, swatch tiles and list rows
        ink: #ffffff, names, figures and IDs
        muted: #b7bfcb, tile titles, notes and axis
        rule: #2c323c, the neutral band, grid lines and row rules
        signalBlue: #38bdf8, the request line, p50, the current app, the primary button, the deploys band and the focus ring
        healthy: #4ade80, the Healthy band, word and circle, and Resolved with a square
        degraded: #fbbf24, the Degraded band, word and triangle, the incident band, p95 and Investigating
        recovered: #7cb8ff, the Recovered band, word and diamond
        firing: #ff7a7a, Firing with an octagon, the error and alerts bands and the error line
    type:
        Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial at 600 to 800. Base 16px at
        1.35. The incident ID is 60px at 800, service figures scale from 40
        to 52px at 800 with tabular numbers, status words scale from 22 to
        34px at 800 in caps, service names 30px at 800, notes 20px, tile
        titles 18px caps tracked 0.08em.
    layout:
        A full bleed six column wall with 4px black bezels and no outer
        margin. A raised title strip holds BRIGHTWORK OPS, PRODUCTION LAST
        24 H and the suite apps as flat blocks with Ops in signal blue. A
        row of five service screens follows, each with a 10px status band on
        top in green, amber or blue, the name, a huge status shape and word,
        a giant uptime figure and one fact, billing showing 6 MIN DOWN. Then
        a four column Requests per minute screen with a 44px peak figure and
        a 6px line chart, beside a two column incident screen with an amber
        band, a 60px INC-0427, the title, status, opened, owner and large
        buttons. Then Error rate and Latency screens with big figures and
        5px lines, and an Alerts screen with a red band. A full width
        Deploys screen with a blue band lists the three deploys with 32px
        times. Below 1180px services go three across and charts widen,
        below 760px every screen stacks in one column.
    spacing: 4px bezels between every screen, 18 to 20px tile padding, no outer margin beyond one bezel.
    density: Low in items and high in size. Every tile holds one idea at wall scale.
    corners: None anywhere, like display panels.
    borders: A 10px status band across the top of each tile in green, amber, blue or red, and 2px rules inside lists.
    shadows: None. Black bezels separate screens.
    icons:
        Filled status shapes at about 1.3 times the status word, a circle
        for Healthy, a triangle for Degraded, a diamond for Recovered, an
        octagon for Firing, a square for Resolved and a magnifier for
        Investigating. Chart lines are 5 to 6px.
    focus: An inset 4px white ring plus an 8px signal blue inner ring, drawn inside tiles so bezels never hide it.
    tone: Short caps labels for distance, such as INCIDENT SEVERITY 2, PEAK and MS P95.
